<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Did the Jazz Extend Jaren Jackson Jr.?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Jackson is paid <strong>$49m</strong> because Memphis extended him before he could reach free agency, and a trade carries that contract across unchanged.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went fourth in 2018 and his rookie contract was worth <strong>$29.28m</strong>.</li>
<li>Memphis extended him in 2021 for <strong>$104.72m</strong> across four years.</li>
<li>That deal’s last season was renegotiated upward by <strong>$11.59m</strong> to <strong>$35m</strong>.</li>
<li>The new extension is <strong>$205m</strong> over four years, fully guaranteed.</li>
<li>His salary rose by <strong>$14m</strong> between last season and this one.</li>
</ul>
<p>He takes up more than a quarter of what Utah spends.</p>

