<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/jaren-jackson-jr/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/jaren-jackson-jr/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Jaren Jackson Jr.’s Salary With the Jazz?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Jackson earns $49m in 2026-27, the largest salary at Utah and the first year of a four-year extension. It rises from $35m last season. His career earnings come to $194.59m across nine seasons. The salary is 26.78% of the club’s $182.97m payroll, so more than a quarter of what Utah spends goes to one player."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What’s Next for Jaren Jackson Jr. Beyond 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Two more guaranteed seasons follow this one, then a player option on 2029-30. Declining it would put him in free agency at 30."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Does Jaren Jackson Jr. Earn Over Time?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A $49m season is hard to picture, so here's what it comes to over smaller stretches of time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When Does Jaren Jackson Jr.’s Contract Expire?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Jackson signed a four-year extension worth $205m with Memphis in 2025, all of it guaranteed. Utah took it on when it traded for him. The final season is a player option. He would reach free agency in 2030 at 30."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Jaren Jackson Jr.’s Estimated Net Worth?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Jackson’s net worth is estimated at around $77.84m, taken from his $194.59m in career earnings. One outlet puts him at $15m, which is under a twelfth of what he has been paid and predates this extension. He played one season at Michigan State and Memphis took him fourth in 2018, three months before he turned 19."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why Did the Jazz Extend Jaren Jackson Jr.?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Jackson is paid $49m because Memphis extended him before he could reach free agency, and a trade carries that contract across unchanged. He takes up more than a quarter of what Utah spends."}}]}</script>
